30,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, the firms flagged clay and slippage. The depot says we can hoard the south, but not the center.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, that confirms my fear. The ground is already stressed; adding heavy machinery to unstable clay is a recipe for disaster.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found the staff numbers dropped a lot, but there are two volunteer groups ready to help.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Minako,,"- **Minako**: The basin held, but the apron failed. And half the avenue trees died from neglect.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The fund pays only for planting and water, never surfacing or buildings. The ledger confirms planted ground costs triple to maintain.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Minako, that’s worrying. If the trees died from neglect, how do we trust the new planting to survive?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the clay is a risk, but the heat data is worse. The ground is already failing under current conditions.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Minako, that is sad. But the volunteer groups are there. I hope they can help with the watering so the trees don’t die again.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, volunteers are a bonus, not a contract. I need to know if the city commits to the aftercare this time, or if we repeat the mistake.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, exactly. If the fund excludes surfacing, we are left paying triple for the planting while the hard surfaces crumble.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, the clay is bad, but the depot notes say we can hoard the south. Can we build there without touching the unstable center?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the counts show people stick to firm ground. If we hoard the south, we block the main crossing. We’d be fighting the daily flow.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Benjamin, that makes sense. If people need the firm ground, we shouldn’t block it. I just worry about who mows the rest.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, the roll is down to seven. If we add water features, we’re buying in specialists. That’s a permanent cost, not a one-off.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, precisely. The fund covers the water, but the ledger shows the city pays triple for the upkeep. We’d be funding a permanent leak.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, if the south is blocked, where do the diggers go? I’m worried we’re stuck with no safe place to start.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the center is the only open space, but it’s the most fragile. We can’t dig there without risking the whole site.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minato,,"@Kenji, I am worried. If the center is too fragile, where do we start? I just want a place that is safe and easy to care for.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Kenji, we start by respecting the constraints. If the center is fragile and the south is blocked, we must design for the margins, not force the middle.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, designing for the margins sounds wise, but if the fund only pays for planting, who pays for the hard paths people actually need?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
57,3,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
58,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, if the center is fragile and the south is blocked, how do we even start digging? I’m worried we’re stuck.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, we don’t dig in the center. We work the margins where the ground is firm, or we accept that heavy earth-moving is off the table entirely.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minato,,"I am confused. If we cannot dig in the middle or the south, where do the new things go?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, the candidates are here. We must pick one that fits our broken ground and thin staff, not just a pretty drawing.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, I see the candidates. I am looking for the one that does not trap us in endless, expensive maintenance.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, if we avoid the center, does that mean we can’t do the big sports courts? I just want to know if we can still build something fun.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the terraces need heavy surfacing and deep foundations. With the clay and the blocked south, that’s a logistical nightmare.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minato,,"I am worried. If the sports courts are too hard to build, what is left? I just want a place that is easy to keep clean.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, the woodland walk fits the northern margins. It avoids the fragile center and the blocked south, and the fund covers the planting.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, the fund covers the planting, but the ledger says it costs triple to maintain. We’d be signing up for a permanent financial drain.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Minako, but if the trees died before, how do we know the woodland walk won’t just be a graveyard? I need to know if the ground can hold them.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the avenue failed due to missing aftercare, not bad soil. If we contract for watering, the woodland is viable. The wetland is the real risk.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minato,,"@Benjamin, that is good to hear. But with only seven staff, can we really manage the watering? I am worried about the extra work.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, the volunteer groups handle habitat tasks upriver. We contract the watering, and they help. It’s manageable if we commit to the aftercare.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, the fund pays for the planting, but the ledger shows the city pays triple for the upkeep. We’d be funding a permanent leak.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, so if we contract the watering, the trees live? I just want to make sure we don’t end up with dead wood again.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, yes, if the contract is explicit. The wetland is the trap; the woodland is the compromise. Vote for the walk, not the ponds.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minato,,"@Benjamin, I am still worried about the work. But if the volunteers help, maybe it is okay. I will vote for the woodland walk.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Minako,,"@Jonathan, the triple cost is real, but the wetland is worse. The walk is the only option that fits our broken ground and thin staff.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I vote for the woodland walk. It is the only plan that does not trap us in a permanent, expensive leak.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
